The client ping value is the keepalive round-trip time through the actual Twingate path. Packet culling and TCP tuning reduce bandwidth, bufferbloat and server work, but they cannot guarantee a drop from 230 ms to 120-150 ms if the tunnel/ISP route itself is 230 ms. A guaranteed 120-150 ms from Bangladesh needs a server host closer to the players (Singapore/India/Bangladesh VPS), not a GitHub Actions runner in the US. I did not claim a measured real-world ping improvement because the end-to-end Twingate path was not benchmarked from here.
